						<div style="width:100%;">
							<span style="FONT-SIZE: 36pt; FONT-FAMILY: Argos; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 36pt; FONT-FAMILY: Argos; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><strong><font color="#ffc0cb" size="6">Brangvyne Nimloth</font></strong></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 36pt; FONT-FAMILY: Argos; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><strong><font color="#ffc0cb"><font size="4"> <hr id="null" /> <?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /><o:p></o:p></font></font></strong></span> <p></p><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Argos; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#ffc0cb"><font size="4"> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">It is not known exactly where Brangvyne was born, or to whom, or precisely how she came to be left as a child alone and weeping in the forest of Greater Faydark near the city of Kelethin. Nor can Brangvyne, or Bran, as she is generally called fill in much of the detail. In her waking thoughts she can sometimes picture a pair of liquid blue eyes gazing down at her, soft hands gently caressing her, and a soft warm breast where she felt snug and safe. Her dreams are darker though; filled with screams, hot red flames searing her, and the twisted snarling of dark evil orcish faces.</span><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Arial Unicode MS'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Arial Unicode MS'"><o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">Rescued, as she was at this tender age adrift in the land of Norrath by a kindly druid, Bran grew up in the deep and wild places of Norrath. It was, in fact, widely assumed that she would become a druidess but although she inherited the druids’ love of nature she was not to follow in his chosen footsteps.<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">As Bran entered adolescence several things began to change for her. A willful and stubborn child she often went out of her way to annoy her guardian even while a growing romantic attachment for him began to blossom in her young heart. Meanwhile her interest began to turn more and more toward the life of a ranger. She took up archery, that ancient love of the wood elves, and she began to train under the watchful eye of master Trueshot himself, who in time taught her to create her own elven cultural armor and to her great joy her own Trueshot bow.<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">Now a ranger, although a young one, Bran was given the chance to join in the guild, Hand of Judgment where she would make her home for a number of season to come. Finally that fateful day arrived when she reached womanhood and took for herself the name of Brangvyne Nimloth, or roughly translated, fair maiden of the white flowers. Her passions were hunting and fishing, plying her chosen trade of fletching, and foremost spending time with her mentor, now turned first love, traveling the lands of Norrath.<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">On the surface everything seemed wonderful for Bran, however, it was not so. She was a free spirit and even as she grew close to her mentor and friend and thought of marriage she drifted further apart from him. The older druid seemed too protective and controlling to her. She cared for him, but he was jealous and started to irritate her. She felt stifled. They quarreled often. Finally, after one particularly bad argument the guild officers evicted him from the guild. Soon after they split up.<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">Brangvyne, although saddened by the way things had turned out was already looking elsewhere. It so happened that there was a handsome ranger, who had already caught her eye. Her problem was that he was engaged to a friend of hers; which meant she could not act on her desires. As would happen, not long thereafter, her new interest and her friend separated and she was free to pursue him. In the end this quarry was easily caught and shortly thereafter they wed. Brangvyne left her guild to join his, Obsidian Ryders.<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">For a time they were happy, a pair of rangers sharing life together in Norrath, until one day she found that her husband had left her with only a note explaining that he was going and would likely never return. For a short time she waited hoping he would come back, but such was her nature that it was not for long. Feeling abandoned she changed her name back to Nimloth and returned to her old guild now as an officer to help lead them in their adventures in Norrath.<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">Yet another druid entered her life and a brief courtship and even briefer marriage resulted in the birth of a daughter named Aeowyne Nimloth. Aeowyne was a lovely child and musically inclined. A promising bard, it was a loss to the wood elf community not to mention a grievous blow to Bran herself when young Aeowyne was slain by orcs at a young age and departed the world of Norrath forever.<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">Problems developed in her guild life as well and Bran was deguilded from Hand of Judgment and refused readmission back into Obsidian Ryders. Depressed she joined Val’Kori with some of her friends. In Val’Kori she made new friends and got along fairly well, however, after a brief tryst with a barbarian warrior she never felt she fit in completely and eventually left.<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: pink; FONT-FAMILY: Argos; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA">It was in her wanderings not long after leaving Val’Kori that her dearest friend in Norrath and adopted sister Xenawyr Nimloth invited her to join in a guild that had recently formed. There were several people in the guild she know, old friends joined together once more, and she gladly accepted to invitation happy to have a guild home where she fit in and felt welcome once again. It is here she resides until this day.</span></font></font></span></span></p>
							
